cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the XLGD umbrella mark, cite it as below."
title: "XLGD — X distinction mark for LGD (Lifecycle Governance Doctrine)"
abstract: >-
  XLGD is the umbrella mark for a governance line that fronts a theory (LGD,
  the Lifecycle Governance Doctrine: 凡自治之物 · 有籍 · 有证 · 有门禁), an
  executable protocol (UIBC: registry / evidence / gates), a verifier-side
  catalogue of silent-failure modes, and agent integration skills. The umbrella
  itself is a package identifier for provenance; it is not an independent
  concept and no entity or trademark has been registered.
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: MIT
